WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:01.960
Hi.

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:05.780
Today we're gonna solve a puzzle called the "Triangle Area Puzzle".

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:08.560
What we have is

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:13.280
4 different triangles where the hypotenuse is 3

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:17.560
And the length of 1 leg is 1 unit longer than the other.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:19.720
The question is,

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:22.680
What's the area of a single triangle?

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:26.720
I'm going to give you a moment to solve this,

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:29.520
you can pause the video and take your time.

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:33.680
Once you're ready,

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:35.460
you can keep playing.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:40.920
The answer to this puzzle

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:44.940
is that the area of a single triangle is 2.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.240
The more interesting part, is how we can arrive at the answer.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:54.120
One way you can solve this is you can work algebraically.

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:58.260
This is the long way to solve the problem

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:04.180
The steps involved, are you would label the 2 legs of the triangle as 'a' and 'b'.

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:08.260
You can then set up a system of equations.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:10.600
One equation will be that:

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:12.420
a is equal to b + 1

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:16.860
Because we know that one of the legs is 1 unit longer than the other.

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:19.460
The other equation is that:

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:23.680
a² plus b² equals c², the hypotenuse squared,

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:25.420
in this case 3²,

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:27.640
by the Pythagorean Theorem.

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:30.460
We now have 2 equations,

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:33.080
for 2 unknown variables,

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:35.400
which means we can solve for 'a' and 'b'

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:39.500
and then the final step would be to find the area of a single triangle

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:41.800
which is one half 'a' x 'b'.

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:46.040
This is a rather long and messy way to solve this problem,

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:48.260
I'm actually not gonna go through the algebra,

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:51.240
if you do you'll find out the answer's 2.

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:54.720
However, I want to point out a much more,

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:58.360
elegant way to solve this problem, which is geometric.

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:03.140
So what we're gonna do is start out with these same 4 triangles,

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:07.960
and we can do a little neat trick, where we rearrange the triangles as follows:

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:09.740
We're gonna move one up,

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:10.980
this one to the side,

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:12.760
and shift this one over.

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:15.340
Now we notice something neat:

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:18.140
We basically have a big square,

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:20.640
which has a side 3,

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:22.700
and we have the 4 triangles,

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:24.680
and we have a small square.

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:28.920
From this we can figure out the answer.

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:33.920
We know that the area of the big square is equal to the area of the 4 triangles,

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:35.680
plus the area of the small square.

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:39.680
We can solve the area of the big square, 3²,

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:43.300
must be equal to 1² plus the area of the 4 triangles.

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:46.780
That means the area of the 4 triangles must equal 8,

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:49.500
and the area of a single triangle is 2.

